--TEST--
An argument written as a variable already says what it is, and one written `name:` writes the word itself, so both are skipped and only the bare literal beside them is annotated, `rule:ide/every-feature-is-staged-behind-its-dependency`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Greeter {
    public function greet(string $name, string $tone): string { return $name; }
}
var $g = new Greeter();
string $who = "world";
$g->greet($who, "warm");
$g->greet(name: "world", tone: "warm");
--REQUEST--
inlayHint
--EXPECT--
5:7 type : Greeter
7:17 parameter tone:
